    {
      "id": "claim_a660b607afe04249ba848bf8928152bf",
      "statement": "Callidescope defines five core concepts with precise vocabulary: Callable (function-like declaration traced by file and byte offset), Stack (entry point + deepest path, reports floor when path runs through unresolved call), Depth (frames on stack, entry point inclusive, one of two gated limits), Breadth (distinct direct callees, other gated limit), and Entry Point (callable rooting a stack, declared is only kind a person chose).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CONTEXT.md#L200-L247",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fb6dd0f5a47036d439c1b017d2b311ff33f739a99f336384ff357e328bd1875f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_25a73ea35e3142b49853659f41edbd20",
      "statement": "Callidescope has no notion of a module and measures no cohesion; module spread and possibly misplaced findings were removed per ADR 0006, along with the module identity identifier and four limits that tuned them.",
